  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You have `n` coins and you want to build a staircase with these coins. The staircase is composed of `k` rows where the `ith` row has exactly `i` coins. The last row of the staircase **may be** incomplete.\n\nWith the integer `n`, output *the number of **complete rows** of the staircase you will build*.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n![](https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2021/04/09/arrangecoins1-grid.jpg)\n\n```\nInput: n = 5\nOutput: 2\nExplanation: Because the 3rd row is incomplete, we return 2.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n![](https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2021/04/09/arrangecoins2-grid.jpg)\n\n```\nInput: n = 8\nOutput: 3\nExplanation: Because the 4th row is incomplete, we return 3.\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= n <= 231 - 1`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
